\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.9}{\ignorespaces Expression size per derivative step, log scale. \emph  {simp} holds $a^{*}$ at two nodes but $(a+(b+ab))^{*}$ still grows $\Theta (2^{n/2})$: a straight line on this axis is exponential growth, because at every step the surviving alternation branches are distinct only in their bit annotations, so $\mathsf  {S}_4$ never collapses them. Regenerate with \texttt  {cargo run -{}-release -{}-example thesis\_figures -{}- growth}; \texttt  {tests/test\_thesis\_figures.rs} pins these values.}}{37}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
